        "type": "caption",
        "reading_order": 2,
        "text": "Table 2.2: Datasets used to train GPT-3 . “Weight in training mix” refers to the fraction of examples during training that are drawn from a given dataset, which we intentionally do not make proportional to the size of the dataset. As a result, when we train for 300 billion tokens, some datasets are seen up to 3.4 times during training while other datasets are seen less than once.",
